libseat gives wayland compositors access to the display and input devices without
needing to run as root: it talks to the seatd daemon, or uses its built-in seatd when
the compositor itself has the privileges. This port builds seatd (the daemon and
seatd-launch helper) and libseat with the seatd and built-in backends; logind support
is off. Installs libseat, libseat.h, libseat.pc and the seatd binaries under /usr/local.
The source is the Ubuntu archive's copy of the upstream release tarball
upstream: https://sr.ht/~kennylevinsen/seatd/
